                "reply_count": 2,
                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter Web Client",
                "text": "Today, I introduced the Bipartisan Patient Access to Autoimmune Treatments Act to make it easier for patients with autoimmune diseases and blood disorders to access the medications they need. The bill limits prior authorization requirements under Medicare Advantage and Part D to once per year.\n\nThis commonsense reform has bipartisan support \u2014 just like the version I passed in the Texas State House with Democrats and Republicans, which Gov. Greg Abbott signed into law.\n\nWith the backing of the @AmerMedicalAssn, @texmed, and the @AutoimmuneAssoc, we\u2019re building real momentum. Patients don\u2019t have time for bureaucracy \u2014 and with this bill, they won\u2019t have to.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1758819601,
                "view_count": 396
