                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Twitter Web Client",
                "text": "Before the government shut down last month, I joined my Democratic colleagues in signing a letter to House leadership requesting that Congress fully fund Medicaid Disproportionate Share Hospitals. \n\nWhat did the Republicans do? \n\nThey didn\u2019t just \u201ctighten the budget. They cut $2.8 million in care from Texas\u2019s 32nd District Disproportionate Share Hospitals \u2014 the facilities that care for low-income and uninsured Texans.\n\nThat means longer ER waits. Fewer beds. Less care for kids, seniors, and working families.\n\nIn TX-32, we take care of each other \u2014 and I\u2019ll never stop defending our hospitals and the people they serve.\n\n@NewDemCoalition",
